WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.660
A black hole you can point to.

00:02.425 --> 00:05.388
This is the Swan, flying along the Milky Way.

00:05.867 --> 00:11.616
In its neck is Cygnus X-1, the first thing in the sky that astronomers agreed was a black hole.

00:12.163 --> 00:13.143
You cannot see it.

00:13.427 --> 00:14.312
Nobody can.

00:14.732 --> 00:20.314
It was found in 1964, because it is one of the strongest sources of X-rays in the sky.
